rded as a loner, and no explicit evidence of stress calmness.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** B\u2019s interpersonal drawbacks (pretentiousness, occasional wrong tone, nasty remarks) versus the more severe operational risks of the others (A\u2019s potential crew conflict and lack of stress data; C\u2019s communication deficits; D\u2019s moodiness and isolation). The balance of reliability, stress resilience, and technical weather competence makes B the most suitable overall.\n**Remaining uncertainty:**\n- The severity of B\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and pretentious tone on actual crew cohesion and safety.\n- Lack of explicit evidence of B\u2019s teamwork skills beyond conscientiousness.\n**What would change my vote:**\n- Concrete evidence that B\u2019s interpersonal behavior leads to crew conflict or safety\u2011critical miscommunication.\n- Strong evidence that A\u2019s technical/leadership strengths and any unreported calmness outweigh his interpersonal issues, or that C\u2019s communication difficulties are minor in practice.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}"}
